Diagnostic and correctness fixes for FireSim on the Alveo U55C.
Applies on top of 0001-rebase-target-cycle-counter.patch.

  1. simif_vitis.cc: hold the host_mem_0 xrt::bo as a member. Upstream
     allocates it as a constructor local, so the device allocation is freed
     when the constructor returns and XRT may reassign that memory for the
     entire life of the simulation.

  2. simif_vitis.cc: drop the hardcoded U250 DDR base assertion. The kernel's
     host_mem_0_offset register is IP-XACT metadata only -- it is absent from
     the generated RTL, and writing it lands in FireSim's own widget MMIO
     space. Address mapping is done by the platform memory subsystem via
     --connectivity.sp.

  3. simulation.{h,cc}: add +memcheck, which round-trips a known pattern
     through the LoadMem widget before target execution, testing the target
     DRAM path independently of the design under test. This is what identified
     the U55C HBM memory path as non-functional while the control plane works
     (see docs/proposals/firesim_vitis_host_mem_offset.md).

